        "id": "2112604520857375167",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Austin Justice",
        "text": "UPDATE: Alonzo Mabry is dead.\n\nIn March, the 62-year-old was using a computer at Austin's Central Library when the man next to him, Daniel Vasquez, stood up, hit him in the head, and stomped on his skull while he lay unconscious. Then Vasquez went back to his computer.\n\nMabry died in hospice and Vasquez was charged with murder last week.\n\nBefore the library, Vasquez had punched a CapMetro bus driver in the mouth. That was dismissed by prosecutors.\n\nHe also punched a mother in the face in front of her 11-year-old son, then punched the woman who tried to stop him. Those were also dismissed.\n\nDA Jose Garza's office sent him to a six-month rehab program instead. He finished in June 2025 and every charge was wiped and he went back to the street.",
        "url": "https://x.com/AustinJustice/status/2112604520857375167",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
